n practice, a DTC/NSCC member, typically a broker-dealer) that has an agreement with the ETF or its service provider. The ETF's basket and creation/redemption mechanics must work through that clearing infrastructure.\n\n**Written agreement:** The rule's definition contemplates an agreement with the ETF or a service provider, but it doesn't prescribe the AP agreement's content. Market practice covers creation/redemption procedures, settlement timing, transmittal of baskets and cash, and indemnities.\n\n**Comparing the bank's forms:** Check (1) which entity is the contracting party (the ETF, its trust, sponsor, or distributor), (2) whether the bank is a DTC/NSCC participant or uses a clearing agent, and (3) whether the forms cover custom baskets and settlement mechanics.","ttft_ms":6071,"type":"result","duration_ms":8023,"uuid":"a94dbffa-101a-44ae-a900-af4867eea8ca","ttft_stream_ms":415,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":415,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
